@@ -2,6 +2,26 @@

 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys live in the data
+as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`. Roles:
+
+- `viewer`: reading (`GET`) only.
+- `cook`: reading, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+No key or an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`; a known key without
+permission answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request other than `GET` is audited, allowed or not, with
+`{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }` (`keyName` is null without a
+valid key; `path` is without the query string). `GET /audit` lists the
+entries newest first; managers only.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
